                <pb facs="0258" n="248" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg248"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">722.2315/2665: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-16T19:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>524. From the Under Secretary. Your 691, December 15, 6 p.m. I have discussed
                    this encouraging information with my Argentine and Brazilian colleagues. I hope
                    you will do everything possible to expedite a favorable reply. Please let me
                    know as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>In view of the information contained in your telegram under reference, we have
                    agreed to hold in abeyance the suggestions formulated by the Argentine Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs. The acceptance of the 1936 line would be far more expedient
                    from every point of view. [Welles.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
